  "text": "Successfully completed /specify, /clarify, and /plan for migrating cc-track from npm to Claude Code plugin system.\n\nKey architectural decisions Craig approved:\n- Plugin directory structure following Claude Code conventions exactly\n- Separate hooks per event type (no unified dispatcher)\n- Dual versioning with @semantic-release/git (package.json + plugin.json)\n- Templates stay in plugin directory (not copied)\n- Per-project config in .claude/track.config.json\n- Dedicated marketplace repository\n- Manual migration guide (Claude-readable markdown)\n\nComplexity: 60-75 tasks estimated\n- Major restructuring but preserves all functionality\n- All 366 existing tests must be updated for new import paths\n- Removes compiled binary approach, uses direct TypeScript execution\n\nCraig explicitly approved architecture after reviewing plan against global CLAUDE.md rules. Ready to proceed with /tasks generation.",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes",
    "TASK_101: Plugin Migration Architecture Approved"
  ],
